Nina P: Ran the sampleapp quickstart with defaults and hit a retry pile-up during a burst test. Getting lots of 429s, then retries queue and CPU climbs. Attaching repro in ticket.

Nina P: Repro: npm start (defaults) + 30 workers each paginating and calling embed+generate. Node v18, JS SDK v0.9.1.

Theo B: Can you paste the retry snippet? Sounds like immediate recursive retry that ignores concurrency slots.

Nina P: snippet:
```js
async function loadPage(cursor) {
  const permit = await connPool.acquire();
  try {
    const token = await auth.getToken(); // we thought this was single-flight but check
    return await client.fetch({ cursor, token });
  } catch (e) {
    if (isRetryable(e)) return await loadPage(cursor); // naive retry
    throw e;
  } finally { permit.release(); }
}
```

Ravi S: That recursion is the problem. Even with single-flight token refresh, retries re-enter and can spawn many waiting frames. Two fixes: (1) change retries to an explicit loop that acquires/releases the same semaphore per attempt, (2) ensure token refresh uses an in-flight promise cache in all SDKs.

Theo B: Agreed. Also the paginator retries ignore "retry-after" headers; we should respect server Retry-After and add jitter.

Nina P: Quick test: changed recursion -> loop and lowered default concurrency from 100 -> 12 in local sampleapp. Burst stopped causing OOM and event-loop lag. But we need a balanced default for onboarding that doesn't surprise power users.

Ravi S: Action items:
- Theo: implement retry-loop in sampleapp + respect Retry-After + jitter
- Theo: add CLI flag `--protect-onboard` (default enabled for local runs) that sets safer defaults
- Ravi: open parity PRs for Python/Go SDKs to add single-flight refresh pattern + Config.MaxConcurrentSequences default 12
- Nina: add repro harness and attach flamegraphs to ticket ONB-1492

docs-bot: Created doc task DOC-856: "onboarding: burst-safety section + recommended limits" assigned to Ravi S.

Theo B: I'll land the sampleapp change today and add a unit test simulating 1% token expiry + 200 concurrent attempts to assert only 1 refresh happens.

Ravi S: Also add telemetry: sdk.client.refresh.inflight and sdk.client.retry.queue_depth so hosted can alert on stampedes.

Nina P: Thanks folks. I'll add the quicknote to the quickstart so users don't run the unsafe defaults by accident.

Theo B: :rocket:
